      "customfield_10012" : "0|i002d3:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "[ probs mostly obsolete - as old and mostly done]",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tUse new stream code in libCURL Stroika code – (really network fetcher code)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tRequest takes Stream for postvalue, and Reponse takes Stream with result. Document the meaning – and how it ties in with Content-Length.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tFor REQUEST this is easy. We can check SEEKABLE – and if seekable source, then use the content-length, and also have FLAG in Request saying ‘atuocompute length’. If automcompute length is true and seekable, we can compute. Else no.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tFor RESPONSE – our IMPL will just return a full memory stream, but in the future we could be smarter and return sooner (maybe option in Fetch call to allow this behavior) – so you can stream out the results of a call…",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tSome of this code can be deferred – and just documetne din TODO section of the NETWORK TRANAFTER library headers…",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
